  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "The current best is config_005 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) at 0.650. The multimodal counterpart config_030 (same settings + resnet50, concat fusion) scored only 0.632, suggesting the image modality is adding noise under simple concatenation. Config_031 changes only the fusion strategy (concat → weighted) while holding all other factors constant (scvi_n200, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool), directly testing whether learned weighting can downweight the weak image signal and allow the multimodal model to match or exceed the RNA-only baseline. This is the cleanest single-variable comparison available to determine whether multimodal fusion has any rescue path with the best RNA encoder. With 2 experiments remaining, resolving this question is critical: if weighted fusion recovers the gap, a multimodal config becomes competitive; if not, we can confidently commit remaining budget to RNA-only refinements. It is preferable to config_006 (scvi+transformer) because two data points already show avgpool > transformer, making that test lower-value."
}

